WEBVTT

00:05:28.004 --> 00:05:30.477
which is coming up
with big ideas and sharing them,

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:32.212
that that'll never go into decline.

00:05:32.236 --> 00:05:33.389
Why?

00:05:33.413 --> 00:05:36.039
Because it doesn't require,
you know, strong biceps,

00:05:36.063 --> 00:05:38.158
and yet there's overwhelming evidence

00:05:38.182 --> 00:05:39.623
that in idea professions

00:05:39.647 --> 00:05:41.983
people experience decline as well.

00:05:42.007 --> 00:05:43.745
They just don't expect it.

00:05:43.769 --> 00:05:46.261
AG: What happens to our
cognitive abilities as we age

00:05:46.285 --> 00:05:47.583
is not straightforward.

00:05:47.607 --> 00:05:51.064
It actually depends on what kind
of mental skills we're talking about.

00:05:51.088 --> 00:05:54.480
Psychologists have long distinguished
between two kinds of intelligence:

00:05:54.504 --> 00:05:56.714
fluid and crystallized.

00:05:56.738 --> 00:05:59.429
Fluid intelligence
is your raw processing power.

00:05:59.453 --> 00:06:01.071
It's basically your IQ,